# Japanese translation of the Dokan Lite screens creators use.
#
# Dokan Lite ships no Japanese language pack — `wp language plugin install
# dokan-lite ja` reports "Language 'ja' not available" — so on a site whose
# locale is ja every seller-facing screen was in English. A client testing the
# listing flow could not find their live products because the tab reads
# "Live", not 「出品中」.
#
# Scope is the 355 strings referenced by the product, order, dashboard and
# settings templates and the dashboard navigation, not all 3,727 in the POT.
# Untranslated strings fall back to English, so anything missed degrades to
# what was there before rather than breaking.
#
# Shipped inside the mk-marketplace plugin and loaded from there, so it is
# versioned and deployed with the code that depends on it rather than living
# as an untracked file on one server. If an official Japanese pack ever
# appears it loads first and these strings only fill its gaps.
